Alternate universe where a pseudo-demonic army based off gog and magog invades Earth through Uzbekistan (hopefully done soon!).
The idea is that after the Yom Kippur war the enemy invades (completely unrelated to Abrahamic religion, although they are the inspiration behind the gog and magog story) Mission 1 takes place in december and you control a single BTR rifle company.

Mission 1: 1973, Sogdiana Iron Wall. An iron wall has mysteriously appeared in an Uzbek valley. You have been recently promoted.
Command your soldiers and secure the perimeter, the civilians are concerned about a "Yajuj and Majuj" certainly these are just stories to scare people.
Rules of Engagement: No civilians, their property, and friendly forces are to be harmed in ANY way. Do not approach the wall before scientific teams arrive. Ensure civilians stay at a safe 5 kilometer distance, send units nearby to move the civilians back.
Synopsis: You deploy and the objective is to surround the wall and move civilians. 2 minutes in the first enemies spawn, they breach the iron wall and a cutscene plays. First platoon opens fire on a few slashers for displaying hostility.
A total of 300 enemies spawn in, you are told to hold the perimeter. 5 minutes in a second company (AI controlled) will arrive, they are in BMP-1Ps, and a F/O team comes with them to call for mortars. A few hundred more enemies spawn and mortars fall upon them. Suddenly a large beast (Storm Beast) breaks the wall in half and the invasion begins in earnest. 
Everyone retreats at the 10 minute mark.
Briefing: You have done commendably under situations no man could even dream of. You are given temporary command of a motor rifle battalion, you will replace your commanding officer who has been re-deployed for endangering his men.
We have determined the enemy is of non-human origin. From now own we will be refering to them as "The Deathless" for their unnatural durability, something you have seen first-hand.
They are heading to the nearest population center, Dushanbe. Delay them at all costs, the lives of half a milion innocents depends on it!
Mission 2 Hisar Valley: You deploy in a narrow part of the Hisar valley in the village of Uzun, the northern road is the only road leading to Dushanbe, the south are farmland and isolated houses. The first ranged enemies appear, wielding bows. Armored enemies (like knights of somekind) appear.
You cannot lose the village, three capture points are on the map, village east, west, and farmland.
Mission 3 Dushanbe: After being pushed back to the outer edges of Dushanbe you are tasked with defending for ten more minutes until strategic bombers can cover your retreat, you will gain an extra tank platoon (tank tutorial), and off map mortars (artillery tutorial)
Mission 4 Alai Valley: Open fields with some rough terrain and impassable mountains, after being pushed out of dushanbe you are promoted again and  you have 3 battalions  defense in depth (basically first part of the map you defend, then you counterattack into a new part of the map, you get to deploy your 3 battalions once every 5 minutes._
you lose the counterattack and are forced further east to the chinese border.
Mission 5 Where Heaven meets earth: The point the Kunlun and Tian mountains meet, introduces conflicting chains of command with chinese artillery taking double the time to call, but you get a lot of howitzers. If you are pushed too much back then militias and border guards in buildings will help. You also lost your tanks due to mechanical failure. Communications are re-established and you find out that the real target is Jerusalem.
